 ### [Mutual Information Gradient Shaping](18669-mutual-information-gradient-shaping.md)
-Mutual Information Gradient Shaping (MIGS), implemented as JacobiNeRF, is a training regularization technique that shapes the tangent space of a Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) to encode semantic correlations between scene entities. Unlike first-order approaches that distill 2D features into 3D radiance channels or treat labels as separate output channels, MIGS aligns the Jacobians of correlated entities to maximize their mutual information under random weight perturbations, enabling efficient sparse label propagation and semantic consensus. When to choose: Not given in the sources.
+Mutual Information Gradient Shaping (MIGS), implemented as JacobiNeRF, is a training regularization technique that shapes the tangent space of a Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) to encode semantic correlations between scene entities. Unlike first-order approaches that distill 2D features into 3D radiance channels or treat labels as separate output channels, MIGS aligns the Jacobians of correlated entities to maximize their mutual information under random weight perturbations, enabling efficient sparse label propagation and semantic consensus.
 
 ### [Multi-Level Neural Scene Graph](19889-multi-level-neural-scene-graph.md)
-Multi-Level Neural Scene Graph (NSG) is a scene representation that decomposes an environment into a graph of static, dynamic, and temporal nodes to model urban environments with moving objects and appearance variations. It distinguishes itself from sibling architectures by explicitly separating the radiance field into a static component $\phi$ and a dynamic component $\psi$, conditioned on sequence-level and object-level latent vectors respectively, enabling the disentanglement of scene-dependent appearance from object texture. When to choose: Not given in the sources.
