 ### [NAN (Noise-Aware NeRFs)](20279-nan-noise-aware-nerfs.md)
-NAN is a burst-denoising method that extends the IBRNet architecture to handle degraded noisy images, such as those captured in low-light conditions, by modifying feature extraction, aggregation, and color blending to be noise-aware. Unlike standard NeRFs that synthesize novel views, NAN fixes an existing view image by leveraging multiple noisy inputs of the same scene. It distinguishes itself from its sibling [MIMO-DONeRF](16217-mimo-donerf.md) and [Point-NeRF Adaptation for Object Manipulation](16395-point-nerf-adaptation-for-object-manipulation.md) by explicitly modeling spatial noise statistics through 3D blending kernels and cross-view variance features, rather than relying solely on single-pixel cross-view consistency. When to choose: Not given in the sources.
